;; ===========================================================================
;; Public-API manifest — CURATED metadata sidecar (rf2-3nbl5.2).
;;
;; This file is the human-curated half of the public-API manifest's
;; single-source design. The generator
;; (implementation/scripts/api-manifest/) derives EXISTENCE + :kind +
;; :facade? from live public vars; it joins those against the
;; :classification map here for the three human-classification axes that
;; cannot be derived from code:
;;
;;   :tier   — the closed Tier vocabulary (spec/API.md §Tier taxonomy):
;;             :front-porch | :advanced | :tooling | :adapter | :testing
;;             | :internal-public | :implementation | :deprecated.
;;             Restrictive-by-default: when ambiguous, pick the MORE
;;             restrictive tier. NOTE (rf2-oekz6s): `:internal-public` means
;;             a SUPPORTED host/tool embedding point (the Xray `mount-<panel>!`
;;             family); `:implementation` means public-for-technical-reasons
;;             only (a cross-namespace / test reach that is NOT a supported
;;             surface — an app or tool MUST NOT depend on it). The two used
;;             to be conflated under `:internal-public`; the split is the
;;             clarity win this bead landed.
;;   :owner  — the canonical owning Spec doc (e.g. "002", "Tool-Pair",
;;             "009", "007") — the "where does the contract live" anchor.
;;   :status — shipping lineage (spec/API.md §Conventions Status).
;;
;; ...plus TWO MORE on `:facade? true` rows only — the FACADE-AUDIT axes
;; (rf2-2hpxo). spec/Conventions.md §Facade policy makes a diff that adds a
;; public var to a facade record FOUR fields in the same PR: tier, owner
;; spec, facade-placement justification, and recommended action. Fields 1
;; and 2 are `:tier` / `:owner` above; fields 3 and 4 are:
;;
;;   :justification — WHY this var is on the facade. For a `:front-porch`
;;                    row, what makes it day-one vocabulary; for anything
;;                    else, why a deliberate single-import re-export beats a
;;                    subnamespace door (Conventions §Keep product facades
;;                    coherent). Conventions is explicit that "it was
;;                    convenient" is not a justification and "every consumer
;;                    calls it on their first hour" is. A blank string is
;;                    refused exactly as a missing one.
;;   :action        — the placement verdict, from the CLOSED vocabulary
;;                    :keep | :rename | :move | :internal-public.
;;                    `:keep` = front-porch, or a justified single-import
;;                    re-export. `:rename` = a lifecycle-verb-law or
;;                    vocabulary violation (the surface stays, the name
;;                    changes). `:move` = it belongs behind an existing
;;                    subnamespace door. `:internal-public` = a host/tool
;;                    embed seam, not a consumer surface.
;;                    `:move` is deliberately RECORDABLE on a live facade
;;                    row: the table must be able to say "this is ruled to
;;                    move" before the move lands. The gate that makes it
;;                    happen is the tracker edge onto the release bead, not
;;                    this file.
;;
;; The generator REFUSES any `:facade? true` row missing `:justification` or
;; carrying an `:action` outside that set, so the diff-time obligation now
;; has a mechanical home rather than living only in PR bodies. Both axes are
;; scoped to facade rows: Conventions puts the obligation on FACADE exports,
;; and requiring prose on all ~528 rows would be a different, larger rule.
;;
;; HAND-EDIT THIS FILE; never hand-edit spec/api-manifest.edn (generated).
;; Adding a public var? Add its [namespace var] entry here, then
;; regenerate. The CI drift-check (lint.yml → api-manifest job) goes red
;; until both this sidecar and the generated manifest are updated.
;;
;; The :classification map is keyed by ["namespace" "var"] (both strings).
;; ===========================================================================
{:meta
 {:doc      "Curated tier/owner/status sidecar for the public-API manifest."
  :keystone "rf2-3nbl5.2"}

 ;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; CLJS-ONLY surfaces — public vars in ClojureScript-only namespaces that
 ;; cannot be `require`d on the JVM, so the generator carries them verbatim.
 ;; Each row is the FULL manifest row, and carries its own
 ;; `:runtime-verified?` flag.
 ;;
 ;; RUNTIME VERIFICATION (rf2-2mtte). The CLJS-side enumeration probe
 ;; (implementation/scripts/api-manifest/probe/, run by `npm run test:cljs`)
 ;; reconciles the LIVE public vars of each covered namespace against these
 ;; rows — the CLJS equivalent of the JVM `ns-publics` existence-check. A
 ;; row whose namespace the probe covers is `:runtime-verified? true`:
 ;;   - the two adapter namespaces (Reagent / UIx) are
 ;;     fully-rowed (their public surface IS the documented adapter API per
 ;;     spec/API.md §UIx adapter), so a var added / removed / renamed
 ;;     there turns the probe RED;
