                                                 :action :keep
                                                 :justification "Facade re-export, optional artefact (Conventions Optional-artefact wrapper convention) -- but epoch is that convention's SILENT-DEGRADE exception, not its raising case. core_epoch.cljc gives this wrapper :on-absent :empty-vec, so an absent day8/re-frame2-epoch artefact returns the empty vector rather than raising; only the write surface replace-frame-state! raises :rf.error/epoch-artefact-missing (Tool-Pair Time-travel Artefact home; the 009 :rf.error/epoch-artefact-missing catalogue row; Conventions Adapter shipping convention Dependency direction). That degrade is only expressible from the ALWAYS-LOADED facade: moving the export to re-frame.epoch would turn a leftover dev-time call site into a hard require failure in a release build that omits the artefact, and would pull the artefact onto the production classpath against Conventions Bundle-isolation conformance. The surface is dev-tier, gated on interop/debug-enabled? and elided by Closure DCE under :advanced + goog.DEBUG=false (Tool-Pair Time-travel Production elision), so the facade row IS the optional-capability and release-DCE seam, not a convenience alias. The epoch query surface is standing-classified tooling at its re-frame.core home row by API.md Tiering of cross-tool surfaces."}
